    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nI'm thinking `mini.statusline` can support similar feature from `lualine` `disabled_filetype` and `disabled_buftype` for setting statusline.\r\n\r\nThis might be a bit hard since lualine manage buffers and render statusline by themselves, whereas afaik mini.statusline uses `vim.o.statusline` (Please do correct me if I'm wrong).",
