        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "All 'mini.nvim' modules can be disabled per buffer my setting `vim.b.minixxx_disable` buffer-local variable to `true` (that is, if disabling module per buffer even makes sense). This is [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d8faae693d266ee4f3a2bf1fb7ca4bc81314c3e9/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L70-L76). For automated disabling, see [recipes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d8faae693d266ee4f3a2bf1fb7ca4bc81314c3e9/doc/mini.txt#L335).\r\n\r\nThis approach was chosen **specifically** to not have to implement all kinds of `disable_*` config entries.",
